cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "VolAnti: an open-source acoustic detector for radio-silent multirotor drones"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Rossen
    given-names: Agam
    affiliation: "University of York, Department of Electronic Engineering"
repository-code: "https://github.com/agamrossen/VolAnti"
url: "https://agamrossen.github.io/VolAnti/"
abstract: >-
  VolAnti detects small multirotor aircraft acoustically, by tracking the
  harmonic comb produced by spinning propellers, rather than by listening for a
  control link. This makes it effective against fibre-optic FPV airframes and
  other aircraft that emit no radio signal. The design is a four-microphone
  array on an ESP32-S3, a four-tier detector stack running every 32 ms, and a
  LoRa peer-alert link, in a printed weather-resistant enclosure.
keywords:
  - acoustic detection
  - drone detection
  - harmonic comb
  - microphone array
  - embedded DSP
  - ESP32
  - open hardware
license: Apache-2.0
